 "notes": "Bourbon: 59 old SKUs folded into 24 archetypes plus 26 leftover models; dropped Ten High (a blended whiskey per Sazerac page), Lasso Motel DARTS Cigarette Blend (novelty SKU), duplicate Willett/O.K.I./Rabbit Hole/Redemption/Starlight SKUs and second Weller entry. Jack Daniel's Tennessee Honey left out (a liqueur). Non-US ryes (Greenbanks, Siderit) kept in Rye m pending a world-whisky home. No Balcones/High West archetypes (pages 404 or not fetched). Kind sources switched from retailer pages to Wikipedia/TTB. No traditions needed. From the Scotch shelf hand-over: Stranahan's Snowflake (already a version) and St George Baller Single Malt added; Frey Ranch 100% Barley Whiskey (Unmalted) and Longleaf Distilling Co. Cask Strength Heirloom American Whiskey left out: neither is bourbon, rye, wheat, corn or malted single malt, so no kind on this shelf fits (suggest a generic American/World whisky home)."
